+// =====================================================================
+// Bugs found by static+dynamic audit in the original tlb.cc.item2.verified
+// (see ~/CS622_L2_TLB/PERFORATED_TLB_REPORT.md "What was wrong earlier"):
+//   bug1 PERF_L2_DEMAP          demapPage() only removed the L1 entry; the
+//                                L2 2MB region's per-4K sub_valid/coarse
+//                                filter bit for that page was never cleared,
+//                                so a later remap of the same VA could be
+//                                served a stale physical address out of L2.
+//   bug2 PERF_L2_FLUSH_NONGLOB  flushNonGlobal() (CR3 switch) only cleared
+//                                L1; stale L2 regions from the old address
+//                                space survived a context switch.
+//   bug3 PERF_L2_PCID           L2 regions were keyed by vpn_2mb alone, with
+//                                no address-space tag, so two processes that
+//                                map the same VA to different physical pages
+//                                would alias each other's L2 translations.
+//   bug4 PERF_L2_PERMS          l2_lookup() reconstructed every hit with
+//                                hardcoded user=true/noExec=false/global=
+//                                false instead of the page's real
+//                                permissions (only invisible in SE mode,
+//                                where those three fields happen to always
+//                                be true/false/false anyway; a real bug in
+//                                FullSystem mode).
+//   bug5 PERF_L2_DUP_INSERT     the SE demand-miss handler called l2_insert()
+//                                a second time for the same page insert()
+//                                already L2-inserts internally; redundant
+//                                work (not a correctness bug, fixed anyway).
+//   bug6 PERF_L2_CHECKPOINT     serialize()/unserialize() never saved/
+//                                restored L2 state; fixed by clearing L2 on
+//                                restore so stale pre-checkpoint entries
+//                                cannot leak across a restore (full L2
